  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-12-01T08:28:58.107Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I'm assuming that this is accomplished by deleting the default 'Members' role. Here are some steps that I did to replicate it:\n\nCreating the group...\n\n- Create an invite only group\n\n- Have private visibility\n\n- Set the new group roles as \"Managed Invite-Only\"\n\n-Finish creating the group\n\nAfter the group is created...\n\n- Delete All the roles that you can\n\n- Create a new role not named 'Member'\n\n- Invite someone and have them join\n\nAfter the person joins, Try to do anything to the user like adding roles.",
